      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-unimaculata-tarakan-yellow",
      "html": "<ul><li>From the Betta unimaculata complex.</li><li>IUCN Red List: Data Deficient.</li><li>Maximum size: 3.5 inches (about 9 cm).</li><li>Breeding: mouthbrooder.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-unimaculata-tarakan-yellow",
      "html": "<p>Wild-caught Betta unimaculata from the island of Tarakan.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-unimaculata-tarakan-yellow",
      "html": "<ul><li>TDS: about 60–100</li><li>pH: 5.0–7.0</li><li>Temperature: 72–82°F (22–28°C). They prefer cooler temperatures, but higher temperatures induce coloration and breeding behaviour.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-unimaculata-tarakan-yellow",
      "html": "<p>Carnivorous. Currently fed live, frozen and dried foods: blackworms, frozen bloodworms and pellets.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-unimaculata-tarakan-yellow",
      "html": "<p>Like many of the species in this complex, with the largest bettas, they can be aggressive. It is recommended to keep them in a species-only tank as they can eat anything that fits in their big mouth.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-unimaculata-tarakan-yellow",
      "html": "<p>Fully grown adult males have longer ventral fins, a larger body and iridescent plating on the cheeks. Females can sometimes have iridescence on the cheeks.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-unimaculata-tarakan-yellow",
      "html": "<p>Mouthbrooder.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-unimaculata-tarakan-yellow",
      "html": "<p>A large unimaculata-type betta found on the island of Tarakan, known for full-colour iridescent cheeks. Also known as Betta ocellata; it is unknown whether they are the same or different species.</p>"
    }
  ],
